# Uniform by-reference capture (B1): a two-level nested closure shares a grandparent local. `inner`
# captures `x` through `make` (CapSrc::Captured), and reading it sees a write made in the grandparent
# scope AFTER both closures were created — proving the cell aliases across two capture levels.
# (Chezzi closures are expression-only, so the inner closure READS `x` rather than the design's
# statement-form `x = x + 10`; the transitive-capture cell path is what B1 exercises.)
fn main():
    x := 1
    make := fn() -> fn() -> int: fn() -> int: x
    inner := make()
    x = 11
    print(inner())          # 11

main()
